  "body": "**Replaces #427**, which was opened from the old fork. GitHub detached that fork from this repo's network when NeoTech/Camcraft was briefly private, so #427 can no longer be updated. This branch also carries the merge with main at #461.\n\n## What changed\n**A new program-entry kind: Pause (M0), Optional stop (M1) and Go home.**\n- Entries sit in the operation list alongside operations, using the same `OperationMeta.order`.\n- The new component `schema::ProgramEntry { action, setup, suppressed }` is not an `Operation`. So `setup::operation_order`, and every walk built on it, skips entries without per-walk carve-outs: the post tool gate and freshness, `rest::ahead_of`, the program sim, the setup sheet, the tool list, verify and `RegenerateAll`.\n- An entry has no generated status, so it never holds the post as \"not generated\".\n\n**Posting.** Each entry folds into the posted op before it, as that op's `PARAM AfterOperation` word (one hook in `posting::op_streams`, logic in `program_entry::posted_afters`).\n- A Pause after Face1 posts byte-identically to setting Face1's after-action to Program stop. This is pinned for all three actions on Fanuc and Haas.\n- Equal asks in one gap merge, and a program stop absorbs an optional stop.\n- An entry after a suppressed op attaches to the last op that posts.\n- Suppress and \"Skip pauses and homes\" mute entries just as they mute op actions.\n- **Refused by name:**\n  - an entry before every posted op;\n  - a Pause and a Home in the same gap (the stream holds one after-word per gap);\n  - entries on the Tormach post, which doesn't read `AfterOperation`, the same as the per-op action there today.\n\n**Commands, all undoable.**\n- New: `AddProgramEntry` (after a named row, or at the end of the active setup), `EditProgramEntry::with_action` and `::with_suppressed`.\n- Reused: `ReorderOperation` (drag) and `DeleteEntity` (Del or the menu).\n- `ReorderOperation`, `CreateOperation`'s append and `DeleteSetup`'s refusal now count over `program_entry::sequence`, which equals `operation_order` on documents without entries.\n\n**UI.**\n- Every operation-list menu gains \"Add pause (M0) after\", \"Add go home after\" and \"Add optional stop (M1) after\".\n- An entry row uses the Post glyph, with its action and SUPPRESSED in the suffix. Its menu offers change action, suppress, delete and add after.\n- Entries drag like op rows.\n\n**Project file: no version rung.**\n- An entry saves as `\"kind\": \"entry\"` plus an `entry` payload.\n- A document without entries writes neither key, so its bytes are unchanged.\n- An older reader refuses a file with entries (serde: unknown variant `entry`) rather than dropping the stops.\n\n**Posted G-code:** only documents with entries change. No `.cps` was touched, and every existing golden is unchanged.\n\n`docs/decisions/155-pause-home-entries.md`\n\n## How tested\n- App `program_entry` (7 tests):\n  - add, reorder, delete, undo/redo, new-op placement;\n  - an entry equals the per-op words byte for byte;\n  - Fanuc and Haas goldens, and the Tormach refusal;\n  - Suppress, Skip and action edits;\n  - the gap rules;\n  - project round-trip, save → load → save byte-stable;\n  - walks unaffected: `program_ops`, tool list, setup sheet, sim verdict, rest digest, verification gate.\n- UI (3 tests): the menu rows; an entry row with undo; a click-through from op menu to add pause, suppress, delete and undo.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick` (app and ui suites) passes except known failures:\n  - `setup_stock_source::a_new_block_after_a_flip…`, red on main (#415);\n  - the headless-GPU ui tests (no adapter on this Mac).\n- `clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --tests -D warnings` is clean. After the merge with main at #410, `program_entry` passes 7/7.\n\n## Not exercised (draft until the contributor's GUI check)\n- A hands-on check of the menus, drag and posted output in a release build. A test kit is prepared.\n- Possible follow-ups:\n  - Home-then-Pause in one gap (needs a compound after-word in every script that reads `afterModes`);\n  - Tormach reading `AfterOperation`, which would change its output for existing per-op documents.\n\nChangelog: Pause, optional stop and go-home entries can be placed between operations in the operation list; they post the same words as an operation's after-action (#155)\n\nFixes #155\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
